# Data contract: $app_name

Generated by lakebase-graph-kit for graph `$graph_name`. The backend reads only the served
views in Postgres schema `$served_schema`, as the role `reader`.

## 1. What exists

### GET /api/walk?start=<natural key>&type=<node type, optional>

Runs the one walk: web, depth $depth, at most $top_n nodes per hop.
It follows edges `$direction`: $direction_meaning.
It follows $edge_types_text.

| Field | Type | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `start.node_id` | string | `$served_schema.node_id_map_view.node_id` |
| `start.node_type` | string | `$served_schema.node_id_map_view.node_type` |
| `start.natural_key` | string | the `start` query parameter, matched to `node_id_map_view.natural_key` |
| `rows[].hop` | integer, 1..$depth | walk hop the node was first reached at |
| `rows[].node_id` | string | `$served_schema.edges_view.$node_id_column` |
| `rows[].node_type` | string or null | `$served_schema.nodes_view.node_type` |
| `rows[].natural_key` | string or null | `$served_schema.nodes_view.natural_key` |
| `rows[].label` | string or null | `$served_schema.nodes_view.label` |
| `rows[].support` | integer | $support_meaning |

Errors: 404 when no node has the key (and type); 409 when the key names more than one node and
no type is given; 422 when `start` is missing or empty.

